From 91ea28e481cd6cd8cc4f5836f5e63741d69806ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:07:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test: coordinates at either end of the wrap interval are
 one point on the circle

A test that coordinates a whole number of periods apart, among them -p/2
and p/2, the two ends of the interval into which each periodic coordinate
is wrapped, are at distance exactly zero: wrapping into [-p/2, p/2) or
(-p/2, p/2) instead passes every other test. Also: the docstring of
_on_circle states the point it returns, R * (1 - cos 2phi, sin 2phi), the
comment on the order of the products says why p / pi is formed apart from
the scale, and AGENTS.md says that the trigonometric functions take one
evaluation per point and periodic dimension. The kernels' code does not
change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
